  "title": "Package M — three priority-0 patterns composed in one package",
  "issuer": "Cedar Valley Robotics, Inc. (synthetic)",
  "scenario": "One credit agreement composes three patterns the register holds as separate defects: (1) 'Guarantor' is defined as 'each Subsidiary that has executed the Guarantee' and 7.01 names both Subsidiaries and Guarantors (a diamond dependency - IPV-21 reports it as a cycle); (2) Amendment No. 1 (effective 2026-04-01) restates 'Consolidated EBITDA' without the income-tax add-back, shrinking the 7.01(c) ratio basket (IPV-19/20); (3) a side letter (effective 2026-05-01) tightens the 7.01(b) general basket from $40,000,000 to $15,000,000 'notwithstanding' the agreement (IPV-16). Authored to see which refusal governs and whether a fail-closed defect hides false permissions.",
  "authorship": "Expectations written by reading the source text. Not derived from compiler output.",
